---
import Operator from '../layouts/Operator.astro';
import { settingsClient } from '../lib/api/client';
const identity = await settingsClient.getNodeIdentity({}).catch(()=>null);
---
<Operator title="Your node" description="Connection and access information for this installation.">
<div class="panel narrow"><h2>Node identity</h2>{identity ? <p style="overflow-wrap:anywhere" class="muted">{identity.nodeId || 'Awaiting node startup'}</p> : <p class="error">Node information is unavailable. Please check that your node is running.</p>}</div>
<div class="panel narrow"><h2>Monitoring preferences</h2><p class="muted">Set the interval, timeout, and enabled state on each monitor. Changes take effect within 30 seconds.</p><a class="button secondary" style="margin-top:20px" href="/dashboard">Manage monitors</a></div>
<div class="panel narrow"><h2>Access and privacy</h2><p class="muted">Your access key protects this dashboard. Sessions expire after eight hours. To rotate the key, stop your installation, replace its access key, and restart it.</p><p class="muted" style="margin-top:12px">Peer networking and automatic location lookup are off in new installations. Node configuration is managed by the installation owner.</p></div>
</Operator>
